<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  One operator's delivery in the Dutch profile (BISON, NL_TT_BASELINE 9.3.0)
  as the national access point publishes it: one document, its stop points
  assigned to quays of the national stop register published apart
  (nl-register/), positions in RD New (EPSG:28992), identifiers of the form
  NL:<operator>:<type>:<code> and private codes beside them (privateCodes).
  No journey lists its passing times: each states its departure and names a
  time demand type, whose run times lead along the timing links its pattern
  names onward from each point — through a timing point that is no stop —,
  with the wait times at a stop point and at a timing point. Line 2 runs a
  loop that passes one link twice, in another time each pass. One time demand
  type states no run time for a link of its pattern. The calendar is
  availability conditions of day bits in the timetable frame's
  contentValidityConditions; the journeys name a day type of the calendar
  frame beside them, which the profile states for information. One journey
  is cancelled on one day, and is written as the profile's own example
  writes it: its condition without that day, a condition not available for
  that day beside it, and a journey naming only the condition not available,
  to show the validity it no longer has. One stop point is assigned to a
  quay the register no longer holds.
  Written for netex-rs's tests (MIT OR Apache-2.0); places, lines and times
  are invented.
-->
